  <static seed="52" source="Contrib/METU-NCC/MAT101/Midterm/line.pg">
    <statement><p>Give the equations for the following lines:</p>
<p><alert> (A) </alert>
Line through the point <m>(2,-2)</m> with slope <m>-4</m>.</p>
<p><m>\qquad y =</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> (B) </alert>
Line satisfying <m>y(-4) = 2</m> and <m>y(2) = -1</m>.</p>
<p><m>\qquad y =</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-\left(2+4\mathopen{}\left(x-2\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2-\left({\frac{1}{2}}\right)\mathopen{}\left(x+4\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
